{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-58108","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68299","text":"Runefort Protocol — v0.1"}]},{"id":"blk-58109","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68300","marks":["bold"],"text":"A layout protocol for living, file-backed, tile-grid web apps."}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58111","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68301","marks":["bold"],"text":"Part of the [&] Protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68302","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68303","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/ECOSYSTEM.md"}],"text":"Ecosystem overview"},{"id":"spn-68304","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68305","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/PULSE/docs/THREE_PROTOCOL_STACK.md"}],"text":"Three-protocol stack"},{"id":"spn-68306","text":" · "},{"id":"spn-68307","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/STACK_COMPLETION.md"}],"text":"Stack status"}]}],"id":"blk-58110","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-58112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68308","text":"Status: draft v0.1 Owner: runefort.com Date: 2026-04-25 Position: protocol-level. Independent of [&], PULSE, PRISM. May be used by them; does not require them."}]},{"id":"blk-58113","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68309","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related documents:"}]},{"id":"blk-58114","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68310","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.core.md"}],"text":"@runefort/core — Reference Web Component Framework v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-58115","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58118","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68311","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/docs/spec/runefort.dsl.md"}],"text":".rune DSL — v0.1"}]}],"id":"blk-58117","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68312","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-BUILD-ORDER.md"}],"text":"Interactive Layer — Build Order"}]}],"id":"blk-58119","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68313","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-1_BYOK.md"}],"text":"RFort-1 — BYOK Modal + OpenRouter Key Storage"}]}],"id":"blk-58121","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68314","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-2_MCP.md"}],"text":"RFort-2 — MCP Proxy + Client + Connection Panel"}]}],"id":"blk-58123","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58126","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68315","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-3_CHAT.md"}],"text":"RFort-3 — Chat Panel with Fort-Aware Navigation"}]}],"id":"blk-58125","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68316","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-4_TOKENFLOWS.md"}],"text":"RFort-4 — Token Flow Animations on Edges"}]}],"id":"blk-58127","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58130","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68317","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-5_REPO_IMPORT.md"}],"text":"RFort-5 — Repo Import → Fort Generator"}]}],"id":"blk-58129","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58132","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68318","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"#/runefort.com/.claude/prompts/RFORT-6_WORKSPACES.md"}],"text":"RFort-6 — Workspace Switcher + Supabase Persistence"}]}],"id":"blk-58131","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68319","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58134","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68320","text":"0. What this is, in one paragraph"}]},{"id":"blk-58135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68321","text":"Runefort is a small declarative protocol for describing a "},{"id":"spn-68322","marks":["bold"],"text":"tiled, file-backed UI layout"},{"id":"spn-68323","text":". You declare *rooms* (tiles), *claims* (file-system regions each room owns), *neighbors* (adjacency for navigation), and *state bindings* (how live state colors a tile). A conformant renderer compiles the declaration to a CSS grid, surfaces each claim's content for inline viewing or editing, and overlays live state. The protocol is the contract between the declaration and the renderer. Nothing more."}]},{"id":"blk-58136","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68324","text":"It is not a workforce platform. It is not a supervisor framework. It is not a graph visualization library. It is the "},{"id":"spn-68325","marks":["bold"],"text":"layout language"},{"id":"spn-68326","text":" that those things can be built with."}]},{"id":"blk-58137","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68327","text":"1. Why a protocol (not a library)"}]},{"id":"blk-58138","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58140","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68328","marks":["bold"],"text":"Renderer-portable."},{"id":"spn-68329","text":" The same "},{"id":"spn-68330","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-68331","text":" should render in Elixir/Phoenix, TypeScript/React, or static HTML. The protocol is the only thing they share."}]}],"id":"blk-58139","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58142","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68332","marks":["bold"],"text":"Diffable."},{"id":"spn-68333","text":" Layouts live in version control as text. Reviews become readable. SVG graph layouts cannot do this."}]}],"id":"blk-58141","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58144","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68334","marks":["bold"],"text":"Extensible by composition."},{"id":"spn-68335","text":" Apps add *vocabularies* (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-68336","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor"},{"id":"spn-68337","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68338","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard"},{"id":"spn-68339","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68340","marks":["code"],"text":"wiki-page"},{"id":"spn-68341","text":") on top of the core primitives. The protocol does not know about supervisors."}]}],"id":"blk-58143","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58146","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68342","marks":["bold"],"text":"No runtime layout engine required."},{"id":"spn-68343","text":" All layout is compile-time deterministic. No d3, no dagre, no jitter."}]}],"id":"blk-58145","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58147","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68344","text":"2. Core primitives"}]},{"id":"blk-58148","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68345","text":"Four primitives. That is the entire vocabulary."}]},{"id":"blk-58149","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68346","text":"2.1 Room"}]},{"id":"blk-58150","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68347","text":"A room is a tile in the grid. It has an id, a position, a size, and arbitrary metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-58151","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"id\": \"memory\",\n  \"position\": [0, 0],\n  \"size\": [3, 2],\n  \"label\": \"memory.ex\",\n  \"meta\": {}\n}"},{"id":"blk-58152","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68348","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-68349","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-68350","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-68351","text":" are integer cell coordinates in a CSS grid. "},{"id":"spn-68352","marks":["code"],"text":"[0,0]"},{"id":"spn-68353","text":" is top-left. "},{"id":"spn-68354","marks":["code"],"text":"size: [3,2]"},{"id":"spn-68355","text":" means 3 columns wide, 2 rows tall. The renderer is free to choose the cell pixel size; the protocol only specifies cell counts."}]},{"id":"blk-58153","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68356","text":"2.2 Claim"}]},{"id":"blk-58154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68357","text":"A claim is a file-system region a room \"owns.\" A renderer uses claims to (a) list which files belong to a room and (b) surface those files inline — either as a viewer or an editor — when the user activates the room. Optional behaviors include generating external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-68358","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-68359","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68360","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-68361","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68362","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-68363","text":") for users who prefer their own tools."}]},{"id":"blk-58155","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"pattern\": \"lib/my_app/memory/**/*.ex\",\n  \"anchor\": \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex#L24\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-58156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68364","marks":["code"],"text":"pattern"},{"id":"spn-68365","text":" is a glob. "},{"id":"spn-68366","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-68367","text":" is the canonical file the room represents (the one a click on the tile opens)."}]},{"id":"blk-58157","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68368","text":"2.3 Neighbor"}]},{"id":"blk-58158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68369","text":"A neighbor declares an adjacency between two rooms. Neighbors drive keyboard navigation ("},{"id":"spn-68370","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-68371","text":"), focus order, and may be rendered as connecting lines."}]},{"id":"blk-58159","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"from\": \"memory\", \"to\": \"deploy\", \"kind\": \"adjacent\" }"},{"id":"blk-58160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68372","marks":["code"],"text":"kind"},{"id":"spn-68373","text":" is one of: "},{"id":"spn-68374","marks":["code"],"text":"adjacent"},{"id":"spn-68375","text":" (touching), "},{"id":"spn-68376","marks":["code"],"text":"linked"},{"id":"spn-68377","text":" (logical link, may not be touching), "},{"id":"spn-68378","marks":["code"],"text":"nested"},{"id":"spn-68379","text":" (one contains the other)."}]},{"id":"blk-58161","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68380","text":"2.4 State binding"}]},{"id":"blk-58162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68381","text":"A state binding tells the renderer how to color a room based on a runtime signal. The protocol defines the *binding*, not the signal source — signals are pushed to the renderer over whatever transport the host app provides (WebSocket, SSE, polling, static)."}]},{"id":"blk-58163","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"room\": \"memory\",\n  \"signal\": \"kappa\",\n  \"thresholds\": [\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.3\", \"class\": \"cold\" },\n    { \"if\": \"< 0.6\", \"class\": \"warm\" },\n    { \"if\": \">= 0.6\", \"class\": \"hot\" }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-58164","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68382","marks":["code"],"text":"class"},{"id":"spn-68383","text":" is a token the renderer maps to CSS. The protocol reserves five canonical classes: "},{"id":"spn-68384","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-68385","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68386","marks":["code"],"text":"warm"},{"id":"spn-68387","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68388","marks":["code"],"text":"hot"},{"id":"spn-68389","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68390","marks":["code"],"text":"fault"},{"id":"spn-68391","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68392","marks":["code"],"text":"idle"},{"id":"spn-68393","text":". Apps may add custom classes — renderers should ignore unknown classes gracefully (treat as "},{"id":"spn-68394","marks":["code"],"text":"cold"},{"id":"spn-68395","text":")."}]},{"id":"blk-58165","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68396","text":"3. Document shape"}]},{"id":"blk-58166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68397","text":"A complete "},{"id":"spn-68398","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-68399","text":" is just an object containing arrays of the four primitives, plus header metadata."}]},{"id":"blk-58167","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"title\": \"my_app forge floor\",\n  \"grid\": { \"columns\": 6, \"rows\": 4 },\n  \"rooms\": [ ... ],\n  \"claims\": [ ... ],\n  \"neighbors\": [ ... ],\n  \"state_bindings\": [ ... ],\n  \"vocabulary\": \"core\"\n}"},{"id":"blk-58168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68400","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.columns"},{"id":"spn-68401","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-68402","marks":["code"],"text":"grid.rows"},{"id":"spn-68403","text":" are the total grid dimensions. "},{"id":"spn-68404","marks":["code"],"text":"vocabulary"},{"id":"spn-68405","text":" is the name of the extension vocabulary in use; "},{"id":"spn-68406","marks":["code"],"text":"\"core\""},{"id":"spn-68407","text":" means no extensions."}]},{"id":"blk-58169","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68408","text":"4. The DSL surface (host-language sugar)"}]},{"id":"blk-58170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68409","text":"Hosts may expose a DSL that compiles to the JSON above. The DSL is "},{"id":"spn-68410","marks":["bold"],"text":"not normative"},{"id":"spn-68411","text":" — only the JSON is. A reference Elixir DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-58171","kind":"code","language":"elixir","text":"defmodule MyApp.Floor do\n  use Runefort.Layout, columns: 6, rows: 4\n\n  room :memory,\n    at: {0, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/memory/},\n    anchor: \"lib/my_app/forge/memory.ex:24\"\n\n  room :deploy,\n    at: {3, 0}, size: {3, 2},\n    claims: ~r{lib/my_app/deploy/}\n\n  neighbors :memory => :deploy\n\n  bind :memory, signal: :kappa,\n    cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\"\nend"},{"id":"blk-58172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68412","text":"A reference TypeScript DSL:"}]},{"id":"blk-58173","kind":"code","language":"ts","text":"const floor = layout({ columns: 6, rows: 4 }, [\n  room(\"memory\", { at: [0,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/memory/**\" }),\n  room(\"deploy\", { at: [3,0], size: [3,2], claims: \"lib/my_app/deploy/**\" }),\n  neighbor(\"memory\", \"deploy\"),\n  bind(\"memory\", \"kappa\", { cold: \"< 0.3\", warm: \"< 0.6\", hot: \">= 0.6\" }),\n]);"},{"id":"blk-58174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68413","text":"Both compile to the same JSON. Either is conformant. Neither is privileged."}]},{"id":"blk-58175","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68414","text":"5. Renderer contract"}]},{"id":"blk-58176","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68415","text":"A conformant renderer MUST:"}]},{"id":"blk-58177","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68416","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-68417","marks":["bold"],"text":"Layout."},{"id":"spn-68418","text":" Render rooms in a CSS grid (or visually equivalent) using each room's "},{"id":"spn-68419","marks":["code"],"text":"position"},{"id":"spn-68420","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-68421","marks":["code"],"text":"size"},{"id":"spn-68422","text":". The grid MUST be deterministic — given the same JSON, the rendered DOM order MUST be stable. 2. "},{"id":"spn-68423","marks":["bold"],"text":"Anchors."},{"id":"spn-68424","text":" Resolve each room's "},{"id":"spn-68425","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-68426","text":" to its content (the file or content region the room represents). Activating a tile MUST surface that content — by default, inline within the host page (viewer or editor). Renderers MAY additionally offer an external-editor handoff URL as a secondary action, but inline surfacing is the canonical behavior. 3. "},{"id":"spn-68427","marks":["bold"],"text":"State classes."},{"id":"spn-68428","text":" Apply CSS classes from "},{"id":"spn-68429","marks":["code"],"text":"state_bindings"},{"id":"spn-68430","text":" to each room's root element. Class names MUST be predictable: "},{"id":"spn-68431","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-cold"},{"id":"spn-68432","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68433","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort-state-hot"},{"id":"spn-68434","text":", etc. 4. "},{"id":"spn-68435","marks":["bold"],"text":"Accessibility."},{"id":"spn-68436","text":" Each room MUST be focusable (keyboard) and have a stable accessible name (the room's "},{"id":"spn-68437","marks":["code"],"text":"label"},{"id":"spn-68438","text":" or "},{"id":"spn-68439","marks":["code"],"text":"id"},{"id":"spn-68440","text":"). 5. "},{"id":"spn-68441","marks":["bold"],"text":"Neighbor navigation."},{"id":"spn-68442","text":" Arrow keys (or "},{"id":"spn-68443","marks":["code"],"text":"h/j/k/l"},{"id":"spn-68444","text":") MUST move focus along "},{"id":"spn-68445","marks":["code"],"text":"neighbor"},{"id":"spn-68446","text":" edges. Renderers MAY also expose mouse navigation; keyboard support is required."}]},{"id":"blk-58178","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68447","text":"A conformant renderer SHOULD:"}]},{"id":"blk-58179","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68448","text":"Provide an inline editor (not just a read-only viewer) for the focused room's "},{"id":"spn-68449","marks":["code"],"text":"anchor"},{"id":"spn-68450","text":" when the host environment supports text editing."}]}],"id":"blk-58180","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68451","text":"Highlight neighbor adjacencies on hover/focus."}]}],"id":"blk-58182","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68452","text":"Re-render on signal change without full reload."}]}],"id":"blk-58184","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58186","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68453","text":"A conformant renderer MAY:"}]},{"id":"blk-58187","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68454","text":"Add domain-specific vocabularies (see §6)."}]}],"id":"blk-58188","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68455","text":"Display additional metadata from "},{"id":"spn-68456","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-68457","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-58190","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68458","text":"Animate state class transitions."}]}],"id":"blk-58192","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68459","text":"Offer external-editor handoff URLs ("},{"id":"spn-68460","marks":["code"],"text":"vscode://"},{"id":"spn-68461","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68462","marks":["code"],"text":"cursor://"},{"id":"spn-68463","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68464","marks":["code"],"text":"zed://"},{"id":"spn-68465","text":") as a secondary action for users who prefer their own tools. Renderers that run outside the browser (e.g. static-site generators, server-rendered HTML with no JS) MAY treat handoff as their primary surfacing strategy and still claim conformance."}]}],"id":"blk-58194","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58196","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68466","text":"6. Vocabularies (extension points)"}]},{"id":"blk-58197","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68467","text":"The protocol's core knows nothing about supervisors, dashboards, or wikis. Apps declare a *vocabulary* — a named bundle of extra fields on "},{"id":"spn-68468","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-68469","text":", extra signals, and extra state classes."}]},{"id":"blk-58198","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{\n  \"runefort\": \"0.1\",\n  \"vocabulary\": \"supervisor-floor.v1\",\n  \"rooms\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"memory\",\n      \"position\": [0,0], \"size\": [3,2],\n      \"meta\": {\n        \"supervisor\": {\n          \"autonomy\": \"advise\",\n          \"uptime_seconds\": 957840,\n          \"last_action\": \"consolidated 47 nodes\"\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}"},{"id":"blk-58199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68470","text":"The "},{"id":"spn-68471","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68472","text":" vocabulary defines what "},{"id":"spn-68473","marks":["code"],"text":"meta.supervisor"},{"id":"spn-68474","text":" contains. A renderer that doesn't know "},{"id":"spn-68475","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68476","text":" MUST still render the layout correctly — it just won't display the supervisor-specific overlay. "},{"id":"spn-68477","marks":["bold"],"text":"Vocabulary unknown = degrade, don't fail."}]},{"id":"blk-58200","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68478","text":"Reserved vocabularies (managed by the protocol authors):"}]},{"id":"blk-58201","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68479","marks":["code"],"text":"core"},{"id":"spn-68480","text":" — the four primitives, no extensions."}]}],"id":"blk-58202","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68481","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68482","text":" — for [&]/Runefort supervisor workforce apps."}]}],"id":"blk-58204","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68483","marks":["code"],"text":"codebase-atlas.v1"},{"id":"spn-68484","text":" — for repository visualization apps."}]}],"id":"blk-58206","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58209","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68485","marks":["code"],"text":"dashboard-grid.v1"},{"id":"spn-68486","text":" — for metric/observability tile dashboards."}]}],"id":"blk-58208","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68487","text":"Custom vocabularies are namespaced freely ("},{"id":"spn-68488","marks":["code"],"text":"com.example.my-vocab.v1"},{"id":"spn-68489","text":"). The protocol does not require registration."}]},{"id":"blk-58211","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68490","text":"7. Non-goals"}]},{"id":"blk-58212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68491","text":"Explicit, so the protocol stays small:"}]},{"id":"blk-58213","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58215","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68492","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a graph visualization protocol."},{"id":"spn-68493","text":" Force-directed layouts, dagre, hierarchies — out of scope. Runefort is grids only. If you need a graph, use a graph tool."}]}],"id":"blk-58214","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58217","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68494","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a state-management protocol."},{"id":"spn-68495","text":" How signals are computed, where they live, how they're transported — host's problem."}]}],"id":"blk-58216","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58219","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68496","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a workforce / supervision framework."},{"id":"spn-68497","text":" That's a *vocabulary* ("},{"id":"spn-68498","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68499","text":"), built on top."}]}],"id":"blk-58218","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58221","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68500","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not a presentation framework."},{"id":"spn-68501","text":" No theming spec, no animation spec. CSS is the renderer's job."}]}],"id":"blk-58220","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58223","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68502","marks":["bold"],"text":"Not coupled to [&], PULSE, or PRISM."},{"id":"spn-68503","text":" A "},{"id":"spn-68504","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-68505","text":" describing a recipe app is fully conformant."}]}],"id":"blk-58222","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58224","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68506","text":"8. Versioning"}]},{"id":"blk-58225","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68507","text":"Semver for the protocol itself. The top-level "},{"id":"spn-68508","marks":["code"],"text":"\"runefort\": \"0.1\""},{"id":"spn-68509","text":" field is the protocol version, NOT the renderer version."}]},{"id":"blk-58226","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58228","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68510","marks":["bold"],"text":"Major bump"},{"id":"spn-68511","text":" = breaking JSON shape change."}]}],"id":"blk-58227","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58230","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68512","marks":["bold"],"text":"Minor bump"},{"id":"spn-68513","text":" = additive (new optional fields, new reserved vocabularies, new state classes)."}]}],"id":"blk-58229","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58232","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68514","marks":["bold"],"text":"Patch"},{"id":"spn-68515","text":" = clarification only, no behavior change."}]}],"id":"blk-58231","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58233","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68516","text":"A renderer MUST refuse documents with a major version it does not support. A renderer SHOULD render documents with a higher minor version, ignoring fields it does not recognize."}]},{"id":"blk-58234","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68517","text":"9. Reference framework — "},{"id":"spn-68518","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"}]},{"id":"blk-58235","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68519","text":"The canonical browser-side reference implementation is "},{"id":"spn-68520","marks":["bold"],"text":"`@runefort/core`"},{"id":"spn-68521","text":": a small set of Web Components ("},{"id":"spn-68522","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-68523","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68524","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-room>"},{"id":"spn-68525","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68526","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-claim>"},{"id":"spn-68527","text":", "},{"id":"spn-68528","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-link>"},{"id":"spn-68529","text":") implementing this protocol with no framework dependency. ~5KB minified target. Specified in "},{"id":"spn-68530","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.core.md"},{"id":"spn-68531","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-58236","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68532","text":"Why a reference framework, not just a renderer:"}]},{"id":"blk-58237","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58239","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68533","marks":["bold"],"text":"Zero-build adoption."},{"id":"spn-68534","text":" Drop one "},{"id":"spn-68535","marks":["code"],"text":"<script type=\"module\">"},{"id":"spn-68536","text":" tag into any HTML page and the protocol is rendered. No bundler, no npm, no framework."}]}],"id":"blk-58238","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58241","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68537","marks":["bold"],"text":"Universal embedding."},{"id":"spn-68538","text":" Custom Elements work inside React, Vue, Svelte, Solid, Lit, Astro, Phoenix LiveView, Rails view templates, plain HTML. The framework adapters are ~1KB each, not full reimplementations."}]}],"id":"blk-58240","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58243","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68539","marks":["bold"],"text":"Single reactivity story."},{"id":"spn-68540","text":" Property setters on "},{"id":"spn-68541","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-floor>"},{"id":"spn-68542","text":" push signal updates; rooms recompute their state class. No virtual DOM, no opinionated state library — composes with whatever the host app already uses."}]}],"id":"blk-58242","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58244","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68543","text":"Conformant alternatives may exist. "},{"id":"spn-68544","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-68545","text":" is the reference, not the only option. A pure-Phoenix-LiveView renderer or a server-rendered static-HTML emitter are both valid conformant implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-58245","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68546","text":"9.1 Authoring surfaces"}]},{"id":"blk-58246","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68547","text":"The same protocol is reachable through three authoring surfaces, all equivalent and all round-trippable:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-58248","spans":[{"id":"spn-68548","text":"Surface"}]},{"id":"blk-58249","spans":[{"id":"spn-68549","text":"Format"}]},{"id":"blk-58250","spans":[{"id":"spn-68550","text":"Use case"}]}],"id":"blk-58247","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-58251","spans":[{"id":"spn-68551","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"}]},{"id":"blk-58252","spans":[{"id":"spn-68552","text":"JSON"}]},{"id":"blk-58253","spans":[{"id":"spn-68553","text":"Programmatic generation, tooling integration, canonical persistence"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58254","spans":[{"id":"spn-68554","marks":["code"],"text":"<rune-*>"},{"id":"spn-68555","text":" HTML"}]},{"id":"blk-58255","spans":[{"id":"spn-68556","text":"Custom Elements"}]},{"id":"blk-58256","spans":[{"id":"spn-68557","text":"Hand-written pages, embedding inside existing apps"}]}],[{"id":"blk-58257","spans":[{"id":"spn-68558","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-68559","text":" DSL"}]},{"id":"blk-58258","spans":[{"id":"spn-68560","text":"Curly-brace declarative"}]},{"id":"blk-58259","spans":[{"id":"spn-68561","text":"Hand-authored layouts, version control reviewability"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-58260","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68562","text":"The DSL is specified in "},{"id":"spn-68563","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dsl.md"},{"id":"spn-68564","text":". The CLI converts losslessly between all three."}]},{"id":"blk-58261","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68565","text":"9.2 Planned tree"}]},{"id":"blk-58262","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"runefort/\n  spec/\n    runefort.protocol.md       ← this document\n    runefort.core.md           ← @runefort/core web component spec\n    runefort.dsl.md            ← .rune DSL spec\n    schema.json                ← JSON schema for runefort.json\n  packages/\n    core/                      ← @runefort/core (web components, target ≤5KB)\n    cli/                       ← runefort CLI (compile/fmt/to-rune)\n    react/                     ← @runefort/react adapter (~1KB)\n    vue/                       ← @runefort/vue adapter\n    svelte/                    ← @runefort/svelte adapter\n    liveview/                  ← @runefort/liveview adapter\n  examples/\n    no-framework/              ← raw HTML, proves \"runs anywhere\"\n    supervisor-floor/          ← the [&] use case, proves supervisor-floor.v1\n    codebase-atlas/            ← non-[&], proves genericity\n    dashboard-grid/            ← non-[&], proves genericity"},{"id":"blk-58263","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68566","text":"Two non-[&] examples are required before we cut v0.1 final. Otherwise we're an [&] dashboard with a spec attached."}]},{"id":"blk-58264","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68567","text":"9.3 Build order (v0.1)"}]},{"id":"blk-58265","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68568","text":"1. "},{"id":"spn-68569","marks":["code"],"text":"@runefort/core"},{"id":"spn-68570","text":" — the four web components + "},{"id":"spn-68571","marks":["code"],"text":"mount(json)"},{"id":"spn-68572","text":". Smallest meaningful artifact. 2. Playground at runefort.com — live "},{"id":"spn-68573","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-68574","text":" editor → rendered floor. The shareable demo. 3. CLI compile path — "},{"id":"spn-68575","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-68576","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-68577","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-68578","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-68579","marks":["code"],"text":".rune"},{"id":"spn-68580","text":" → static HTML. 4. Adapters — React, then LiveView, then others as demand appears."}]},{"id":"blk-58266","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68581","text":"Adapters wait until non-zero users exist. Shipping all adapters before having users is the wrong direction of optimization."}]},{"id":"blk-58267","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68582","text":"10. Relationship to the [&] stack"}]},{"id":"blk-58268","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68583","text":"Runefort is "},{"id":"spn-68584","marks":["bold"],"text":"independent of"},{"id":"spn-68585","text":" [&]. It does not import, depend on, or require any [&] protocol. However:"}]},{"id":"blk-58269","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58271","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68586","marks":["code"],"text":"[&]"},{"id":"spn-68587","text":" capability descriptors MAY be embedded in "},{"id":"spn-68588","marks":["code"],"text":"meta"},{"id":"spn-68589","text":" under "},{"id":"spn-68590","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68591","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-58270","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58273","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68592","text":"PULSE manifest phases MAY drive room generation in tooling that bridges PULSE → Runefort."}]}],"id":"blk-58272","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58275","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68593","text":"PRISM scores MAY be a signal source for state bindings."}]}],"id":"blk-58274","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58276","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68594","text":"These are *integration patterns*, not protocol requirements. A Runefort layout that knows nothing about [&] is fully conformant."}]},{"id":"blk-58277","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-68595","text":"11. Open questions for v0.2"}]},{"id":"blk-58278","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58280","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68596","marks":["bold"],"text":"Nesting."},{"id":"spn-68597","text":" A room inside a room (zoomable). Worth adding to core, or push to a vocabulary?"}]}],"id":"blk-58279","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58282","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68598","marks":["bold"],"text":"Streaming layout edits."},{"id":"spn-68599","text":" Today the JSON is whole-document. Should there be a patch format?"}]}],"id":"blk-58281","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58284","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68600","marks":["bold"],"text":"Manifest discovery."},{"id":"spn-68601","text":" Does a renderer auto-discover "},{"id":"spn-68602","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.json"},{"id":"spn-68603","text":" in a repo, or is the path always provided?"}]}],"id":"blk-58283","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-58286","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68604","marks":["bold"],"text":"Multiple anchors per room."},{"id":"spn-68605","text":" Today one anchor. Real codebases have N files per logical region."}]}],"id":"blk-58285","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-58287","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68606","text":"These are explicitly deferred. v0.1 ships with the four primitives and nothing else."}]},{"id":"blk-58288","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68607","text":"---"}]},{"id":"blk-58289","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-68608","text":"*This spec is the contract. Everything in "},{"id":"spn-68609","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.com/docs/spec/README.md"},{"id":"spn-68610","text":" (the spatial-cognition / dark-factory spec) is now reframed as the "},{"id":"spn-68611","marks":["code"],"text":"supervisor-floor.v1"},{"id":"spn-68612","text":" vocabulary plus the "},{"id":"spn-68613","marks":["code"],"text":"runefort.dark_factory"},{"id":"spn-68614","text":" reference application — both built on top of this protocol.*"}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaieraus6u2kopxnloayvflu3fqkv2oybatej2d5hsykriy5dqtavbnn7a","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}